# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains how to use the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") to implement quantum algorithms directly in fermionic space, rather than mapping to qubits first.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapaliwanag ng gabay na ito kung paano gamitin ang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") para direktang ipatupad ang mga quantum algorithm sa fermionic space, imbes na i-map muna sa mga qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why use fermionic circuits {#why-use-fermionic-circuits}"
msgstr "Bakit gagamit ng mga fermionic circuit {#why-use-fermionic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the traditional workflow for implementing the time evolution of a fermionic Hamiltonian on a qubit-based architecture:\n"
msgstr "Isaalang-alang ang tradisyonal na workflow para ipatupad ang time evolution ng isang fermionic Hamiltonian sa isang arkitekturang nakabatay sa qubit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the fermionic Hamiltonian (for example, $H = \\sum_{pq} h_{pq} c^\\dagger_p c_q$).\n"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang fermionic Hamiltonian (halimbawa, $H = \\sum_{pq} h_{pq} c^\\dagger_p c_q$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map it to a qubit operator (for example, by using the Jordan-Wigner mapping).\n"
msgstr "I-map ito sa isang qubit operator (halimbawa, gamit ang Jordan-Wigner mapping).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement the time evolution in qubit space (using Trotterization or other methods).\n"
msgstr "Ipatupad ang time evolution sa qubit space (gamit ang Trotterization o iba pang paraan).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach has a fundamental limitation; early mapping to qubits discards problem-aware knowledge about the fermionic structure. Standard optimization passes cannot exploit fermionic symmetries or allowed term reorderings, resulting in suboptimal circuits with unnecessary depths and gate counts.\n"
msgstr "May pangunahing limitasyon ang pamamaraang ito; ang maagang pag-map sa mga qubit ay nagtatapon ng kaalamang may kinalaman sa problema tungkol sa fermionic na estruktura. Hindi magagamit ng mga karaniwang optimization pass ang mga fermionic symmetry o ang mga pinahihintulutang pag-aayos muli ng mga term, kaya nagreresulta ito sa mga suboptimal na circuit na may hindi kinakailangang depth at bilang ng gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") enables a better workflow:\n"
msgstr "Nagbibigay ang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") ng mas magandang workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implement the time evolution directly in fermionic space using fermionic gates.\n"
msgstr "Ipatupad ang time evolution nang direkta sa fermionic space gamit ang mga fermionic gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map to qubit space as part of the transpilation process.\n"
msgstr "I-map sa qubit space bilang bahagi ng proseso ng transpilation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach addresses the limitation by keeping problem-aware knowledge in fermionic space, where optimization passes can exploit fermionic structure and commutation relations to reduce circuit depth. The fermionic circuit describes what computation to perform, while transpilation handles how to map it to qubits, providing a cleaner separation of concerns.\n"
msgstr "Tinutugunan ng pamamaraang ito ang limitasyon sa pamamagitan ng pagpapanatili ng kaalamang may kinalaman sa problema sa fermionic space, kung saan magagamit ng mga optimization pass ang fermionic na estruktura at mga commutation relation para bawasan ang circuit depth. Inilalarawan ng fermionic circuit kung anong computation ang gagawin, habang ang transpilation naman ang bahala kung paano ito i-map sa mga qubit, kaya mas malinis ang paghihiwalay ng mga responsibilidad.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generic mode indexing {#generic-mode-indexing}"
msgstr "Generic na mode indexing {#generic-mode-indexing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both the [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module and the [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") use generic mode-based indexing that makes no assumptions about the nature of the modes. A mode is simply an abstract index labeling a fermionic degree of freedom, with no inherent semantics. This design choice mirrors the operators module and ensures maximum flexibility. For example, you can implement time evolution for any operator implementing the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, regardless of its mathematical representation.\n"
msgstr "Parehong gumagamit ang [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module at ang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") ng generic na mode-based indexing na walang ipinapalagay tungkol sa likas na katangian ng mga mode. Ang mode ay isa lang abstract na index na nagtatakda sa isang fermionic degree of freedom, na walang likas na semantika. Ginagaya ng desisyong ito sa disenyo ang operators module at tinitiyak ang pinakamataas na flexibility. Halimbawa, maaari mong ipatupad ang time evolution para sa anumang operator na nagpapatupad ng [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, anuman ang matematikal nitong representasyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a fermionic circuit {#build-a-fermionic-circuit}"
msgstr "Gumawa ng fermionic circuit {#build-a-fermionic-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below implements the time evolution described in the previous section. It constructs a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") by specifying the number of fermionic modes, then adds fermionic gates from the [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") to implement the time evolution.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapatupad ng halimbawa sa ibaba ang time evolution na inilarawan sa nakaraang seksyon. Gumagawa ito ng [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") sa pamamagitan ng pagtukoy sa bilang ng mga fermionic mode, pagkatapos ay nagdaragdag ng mga fermionic gate mula sa [`qiskit_fermions.circuit.library`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library#module-qiskit_fermions.circuit.library \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library\") para ipatupad ang time evolution.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example also demonstrates how to incorporate domain knowledge into an operator by using [operator term grouping](grouping#grouping-explanation). By assigning group indices to the Hamiltonian terms, you preserve structural information that optimization passes can exploit throughout the transpilation stack.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita rin ng halimbawa kung paano maglagay ng domain knowledge sa isang operator gamit ang [operator term grouping](grouping#grouping-explanation). Sa pagtatalaga ng mga group index sa mga term ng Hamiltonian, napapanatili mo ang estrukturang impormasyon na magagamit ng mga optimization pass sa buong transpilation stack.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A simple \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a single time evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-2.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A simple \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a single time evolution gate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-2.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A decomposed \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with several time evolution gates.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-3.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A decomposed \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with several time evolution gates.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-3.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Notice how the operator term grouping is preserved even in simple operations like decomposition. This demonstrates how structural information flows through the circuit stack. To understand the full transpilation to qubits, refer to the [Transpiling fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide.\n"
msgstr "Pansinin kung paanong napapanatili ang operator term grouping kahit sa mga simpleng operasyon tulad ng decomposition. Ipinapakita nito kung paano dumadaloy ang estrukturang impormasyon sa circuit stack. Para maunawaan ang buong transpilation papunta sa mga qubit, tingnan ang gabay na [Transpiling fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep gates apart with a barrier {#keep-gates-apart-with-a-barrier}"
msgstr "Paghiwalayin ang mga gate gamit ang barrier {#keep-gates-apart-with-a-barrier}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The optimization passes fuse neighboring gates where they can. For example, [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") combines a run of consecutive [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates into one, and [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") folds an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") into the rotation that follows it.\n"
msgstr "Pinagsasama ng mga optimization pass ang mga magkatabing gate hangga't maaari. Halimbawa, pinagsasama ng [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") ang sunud-sunod na [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") na mga gate sa isa, at isinasama naman ng [`MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-slater-determinant-preparation#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeSlaterDeterminantPreparation\") ang isang [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") sa rotation na kasunod nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use [`FermionicCircuit.barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") when you want to prevent that. A barrier carries no unitary effect, so it does not change the state your circuit prepares; it only marks a point that the passes do not fuse across. Call it without arguments to span every mode, or pass the modes to restrict it to:\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang [`FermionicCircuit.barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") kapag gusto mong pigilan iyon. Walang unitary na epekto ang barrier, kaya hindi nito binabago ang state na inihahanda ng circuit mo; nagmamarka lang ito ng punto na hindi tatawirin ng mga pass sa pagsasama. Tawagin ito nang walang argumento para sakupin ang lahat ng mode, o ipasa ang mga mode para limitahan ito sa mga iyon:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a barrier separating two orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-5.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with a barrier separating two orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-5.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers survive the fermion-to-qubit transpilation, so they also constrain the qubit-level optimization that follows. The [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide covers that stage.\n"
msgstr "Nananatili ang mga barrier sa fermion-to-qubit transpilation, kaya naaapektuhan din nito ang qubit-level na optimization na kasunod. Sinasaklaw ng gabay na [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) ang yugtong iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat a circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"
msgstr "Ulitin ang isang circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many algorithms apply the same block of gates many times over. Time evolution is the common case: a Trotter step is built once, then repeated to reach the target time. Use [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") to build the repeated circuit, and [`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose\") to join it to a state preparation prefix.\n"
msgstr "Maraming algorithm ang naglalapat ng parehong bloke ng mga gate nang maraming beses. Karaniwang halimbawa ang time evolution: isang beses binubuo ang isang Trotter step, tapos inuulit para maabot ang target na oras. Gamitin ang [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") para buuin ang inuulit na circuit, at [`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.compose\") para ikabit ito sa isang state preparation prefix.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The example below builds a second-order Trotter step for a Fermi-Hubbard model. The step is symmetric: it splits the hopping term into two half-duration [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates surrounding the on-site interaction.\n"
msgstr "Bumubuo ang halimbawa sa ibaba ng second-order na Trotter step para sa isang Fermi-Hubbard model. Simetriko ang step: hinahati nito ang hopping term sa dalawang [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") na gate na may kalahating tagal, na pumapalibot sa on-site na interaksyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeating the step and composing it onto a Hartree-Fock reference gives the full evolution:\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-ulit ng step at pag-compose nito sa isang Hartree-Fock reference ang nagbibigay ng buong evolution:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The repetitions are flattened into the returned circuit rather than wrapped in a single gate, so [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops\") counts two rotations per step. That flattening is what makes the redundancy at the step boundaries visible to the transpiler: the trailing half-duration rotation of one step and the leading one of the next are adjacent, so [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") combines them into a single rotation.\n"
msgstr "Pinapatag ang mga pag-ulit sa ibinalik na circuit imbes na ibalot sa iisang gate, kaya binibilang ng [`count_ops()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.count_ops\") ang dalawang rotation kada step. Ang pagpapatag na iyon ang nagpapakita sa transpiler ng redundancy sa mga hangganan ng step: magkatabi ang huling half-duration na rotation ng isang step at ang una ng susunod, kaya pinagsasama sila ng [`MergeOrbitalRotations`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-orbital-rotations#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeOrbitalRotations\") sa iisang rotation.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps and merged orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-10.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps and merged orbital rotations.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-10.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result costs one rotation per step plus one, which is what you get by fusing those half-steps by hand. Writing the step in its natural symmetric form and repeating it produces the same circuit, so the fusion is left to the optimization stage.\n"
msgstr "Ang resulta ay may gastos na isang rotation kada step, dagdag ang isa, na siya ring makukuha mo kapag mano-mano mong pinagsama ang mga half-step na iyon. Ang pagsulat ng step sa natural nitong simetrikong anyo at pag-ulit nito ay nagbubunga ng parehong circuit, kaya ang pagsasama ay iniiwan sa optimization stage.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you need the repetitions kept apart, pass `insert_barriers=True` to place a [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") between them. The optimization passes do not fuse gates across a barrier, so every rotation survives:\n"
msgstr "Kapag kailangan mong panatilihing hiwalay ang mga pag-ulit, ipasa ang `insert_barriers=True` para maglagay ng [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") sa pagitan nila. Hindi pinagsasama ng mga optimization pass ang mga gate sa kabila ng barrier, kaya nananatili ang bawat rotation:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps separated by barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A \\`FermionicCircuit\\` with repeated steps separated by barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/circuit-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The `reps` argument of [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") is a different concept. It subdivides a single [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate into more, shorter factors, whereas [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") duplicates whole circuits. Repeating a circuit that holds one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") only multiplies its total evolution time.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ibang konsepto ang argumentong `reps` ng [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\"). Hinahati nito ang isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") na gate sa mas marami at mas maiikling factor, samantalang dinudoble naman ng [`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.repeat\") ang buong mga circuit. Ang pag-ulit ng circuit na may isang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ay nagpaparami lang ng kabuuang evolution time nito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure fermionic modes {#measure-fermionic-modes}"
msgstr "Sukatin ang mga fermionic mode {#measure-fermionic-modes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") reads every mode out into a classical bit of its own, pairing mode `i` with bit `i`. Use [`measure()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure\") with your own [`ClassicalRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.ClassicalRegister) to read out only some of them.\n"
msgstr "Binabasa ng [`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\") ang bawat mode papunta sa sarili nitong classical bit, na ipinapares ang mode `i` sa bit `i`. Gamitin ang [`measure()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure\") kasama ang sarili mong [`ClassicalRegister`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.ClassicalRegister) para basahin lang ang ilan sa mga ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Passing `inplace=False` returns a measured copy and leaves the original alone, which matters because a measurement is not unitary: a circuit carrying one can no longer be applied to a state vector, so keep an unmeasured circuit around if you also want to simulate it.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagpasa ng `inplace=False` ay nagbabalik ng sinukat na kopya at hindi ginagalaw ang orihinal, na mahalaga dahil hindi unitary ang isang measurement: hindi na mailalapat sa state vector ang circuit na may measurement, kaya magtabi ng circuit na walang measurement kung gusto mo rin itong i-simulate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring here, rather than on the transpiled [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit), is what keeps the sampled bitstrings easy to read. A fermionic measurement names the mode it reads, so every stage that moves modes around ([`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") at the fermionic level, layout and routing at the qubit level) carries the measurement along with it, and the bitstring stays indexed by the mode you asked about.\n"
msgstr "Ang pagsukat dito, imbes na sa na-transpile na [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit), ang nagpapanatiling madaling basahin ng mga na-sample na bitstring. Pinangangalanan ng fermionic measurement ang mode na binabasa nito, kaya bawat yugto na naglilipat ng mga mode ([`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") sa fermionic na antas, layout at routing sa qubit na antas) ay isinasama ang measurement, at nananatiling naka-index ang bitstring sa mode na itinanong mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Unlike [`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#measure_all), no [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") is inserted before the measurements. Call [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") yourself first if you want one there.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Tandaan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Hindi tulad ng [`measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit#measure_all), walang [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") na inilalagay bago ang mga measurement. Tawagin mo muna mismo ang [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.barrier\") kung gusto mo nito roon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Whether a measured bit means what you expect depends on the fermion-to-qubit encoding, which is chosen during transpilation rather than here. Under an occupation-basis encoding such as Jordan-Wigner each mode is carried by one qubit and the bit is that mode’s occupation; see [`FermionicMeasure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-fermionic-measure#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Nakadepende sa fermion-to-qubit encoding kung ang sinukat na bit ay nangangahulugan ng inaasahan mo, na pinipili sa panahon ng transpilation at hindi dito. Sa ilalim ng occupation-basis encoding tulad ng Jordan-Wigner, dala ng isang qubit ang bawat mode at ang bit ay ang occupation ng mode na iyon; tingnan ang [`FermionicMeasure`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-fermionic-measure#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.FermionicMeasure\").\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile fermionic circuits {#transpile-fermionic-circuits}"
msgstr "I-transpile ang mga fermionic circuit {#transpile-fermionic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To implement the quantum algorithm represented by your [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") it must be transpiled to a [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). You can learn how to do this in the [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) guide.\n"
msgstr "Para maipatupad ang quantum algorithm na kinakatawan ng iyong [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\"), kailangan itong i-transpile sa isang [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). Matututunan mo kung paano ito gawin sa gabay na [Transpile fermionic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

